        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Malkovich, David Zayas, John Dahl, Matt Damon, Edward Norton, Julianne Moore, Oscar Isaac\n- Films: Rounders, Empire of the Sun, The Killing Fields, Con Air, Of Mice and Men, Ripley's Game, Knockaround Guys, Being John Malkovich, Shadow of the Vampire, Burn After Reading, RED, Mulholland Falls, Dangerous Liaisons, Warm Bodies, Ghost World, Juno, The Perks of Being a Wallflower, Annie, Suburbicon\n- TV Series: Dexter, Oz, Gotham\n- Roles: Angel Batista, Osborne, Enrique Morales, Lou, Sal Maroni\n- Topics: acting, film producing\n\nFacts:\n- John Malkovich appeared in films including Empire of the Sun, The Killing Fields, Con Air, Of Mice and Men, Rounders, Ripley's Game, Knockaround Guys, Being John Malkovich, Shadow of the Vampire, Burn After Reading, RED, Mulholland Falls, Dangerous Liaisons, and Warm Bodies.\n- John Malkovich produced the films Ghost World, Juno, and The Perks of Being a Wallflower.\n- Rounders is a 1998 American drama film about the underground world of high-stakes poker.\n- Rounders was directed by John Dahl and starred Matt Damon and Edward Norton.\n- David Zayas played Osborne the cop in Rounders (1998).\n- David Zayas is best known for playing Angel Batista on Dexter, Enrique Morales on Oz, Lou the bodega owner in Annie (2014), and Sal Maroni on Gotham.\n- Suburbicon stars Matt Damon, Julianne Moore, and Oscar Isaac.",
